course: dictionary
lesson: 9667
title: Subtraction in context
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Subtraction means taking one number away from another to find what is left. The answer is called the difference. In maths you show it with the minus sign (−), so 9 − 4 = 5 means nine take away four leaves five.
explain: Word problems often hide subtraction behind everyday words. Look for take away, minus, less, fewer, how many left or how many more. «Ella had 15 stickers and gave 6 away» tells you to take 6 from 15, because giving away makes you have less.
explain: The Mock Turtle in Alice's school has silly names for its sums: «Ambition, Distraction, Uglification and Derision» stand for addition, subtraction, multiplication and division. The names are jokes, but the sums are real. Distraction is the funny name for subtraction, so it is the one to take away.
fact: Subtraction means taking one number away from another.
fact: The answer to a subtraction is called the difference.
fact: The minus sign is −, as in 9 − 4 = 5.
fact: Subtraction is the opposite (inverse) of addition: 5 + 4 = 9 and 9 − 4 = 5.
fact: Words such as take away, minus, less, fewer and how many left often mean subtraction in word problems.
exercise: What is 9 − 4? | 4 | 6 | 13 | *5
exercise: Which phrase tells you to subtract in a word problem? | Double | Shared equally | Altogether | *Take away
exercise: Ella had 15 stickers and gave 6 away. How many does she have left? | 21 | 10 | *9 | 6
test: Which operation is the opposite of addition? | Counting | Division | *Subtraction | Multiplication
test: In «Ambition, Distraction, Uglification and Derision», which silly name stands for subtraction? | Derision | *Distraction | Ambition | Uglification
exam: What is the difference between 20 and 7? | 27 | 14 | *13 | 12
